KONOHAGAKURE NINJA ACADEMY — CURRICULUM OUTLINE
Approved by the Hokage's Office

The Academy prepares civilian and clan children for genin service.
Standard course of study:

Year 1-2: Fundamentals
- Village history and the Will of Fire
- Chakra theory; basic control (leaf-sticking exercise)
- Physical conditioning and basic taijutsu stances

Year 3-4: Applied Skills
- Shuriken and kunai marksmanship
- The Academy Three: Transformation, Clone, Substitution
- Trap-setting, stealth, and basic tracking

Final Year: Graduation Preparation
- Sparring and team drills
- Written examination on tactics and rules
- Graduation test (Clone Technique proficiency)

On graduation, students receive the Konoha forehead protector and are
assigned to a three-genin squad under a Jonin sensei. Instructors:
report readiness to the assignment desk. See graduation requirements.
